.TH ISCSI-CFG-SETUP 8 "December 2024" "HA-Lizard" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
iscsi-cfg-setup \- iSCSI Configuration Setup for HA-Lizard

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iscsi-cfg-setup
[\fB--destroy-existing-data\fR] [\fB--dry-run\fR] [\fB--ignore-host-check\fR]
[\fB--no-slave\fR] [\fB--rollback\fR] [\fB--sync\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
The iscsi-cfg-setup script configures and sets up an iSCSI target in an HA-Lizard environment. It is used to perform various configuration tasks including:

- Setting up replication between two hosts.
- Configuring block devices for iSCSI.
- Setting up DRBD (Distributed Replicated Block Device).
- Updating firewall and LVM filters.
- Managing cluster services and synchronization.

The script performs various checks and prompts the user to provide necessary inputs like IP addresses, hostnames, block devices, and replication link speeds.

.SH OPTIONS
The following options are available:

.TP
.B --destroy-existing-data
Deletes any existing data in the configuration setup. This is used for clean setups.

.TP
.B --dry-run
Performs a dry run of the script without making any actual changes. Useful for testing the script.

.TP
.B --ignore-host-check
Ignores host validation checks during the configuration. If set, host checks such as role in the pool are skipped.

.TP
.B --no-slave
Sets the configuration to operate in a master-only mode. If this flag is provided, no slave host is involved in the setup.

.TP
.B --rollback
Performs a rollback operation, restoring previous settings and removing changes applied by the script.

.TP
.B --sync
Synchronizes configuration files between the master and slave servers. This is used when both servers need to be aligned with the same settings.

.SH EXIT STATUS
The script exits with the following statuses:

.TP
.B 0
Success. All tasks were completed successfully.

.TP
.B 1
Error. The script encountered an error during execution.

.SH EXAMPLES
To run the script with all necessary configuration checks:

.nf
$ iscsi-cfg-setup
.fi

To run the script in dry-run mode (no changes made):

.nf
$ iscsi-cfg-setup --dry-run
.fi

To roll back the setup:

.nf
$ iscsi-cfg-setup --rollback
.fi

